WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.460
Good morning, John. 2 weeks ago I woke up in LA with the goal of packing in as much internet creator hang-out time as possible,

00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:10.460
here is my journal of what I've done so far, with all of the sleeping and driving time taken out.

00:00:10.460 --> 00:00:13.820
It all began when a certain German DJ came to my AirBnB,

00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:15.520
then we went to see our friends Greg and Kim,

00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:18.560
had dinner with Jon Cozart, went on a walk around Santa Monica,

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:22.540
shot Not Too Deep with Grace Helbig, had Meghan Camarena and Lee Newton over for dinner,

00:00:22.540 --> 00:00:26.680
"Once a year, they all go to the desert and get naked". [laughing]

00:00:26.680 --> 00:00:29.800
Spent a day with Rhett and Link and shot a Good Mythical Morning,

00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:34.260
then went out to the launch party for Dysh, an app that's like Yelp but for individual dishes at restaraunts

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:36.800
that Ingrid, Grace, Mamrie, and Hannah have been working on,

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:38.700
shot some stuff at SourceFed and then you came to town,

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:41.580
we had dinner, "Hey John, what are you talking about?" "Soccer."

00:00:41.580 --> 00:00:46.240
shot 2 Just Between Us' with Gaby and Allison, got a parking ticket, "So confusing!"

00:00:46.240 --> 00:00:50.400
hung out with Derek from Veritasium, then went to Meghan Tonjes' house to hang out with cool people

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:52.840
and watch creepy YouTube videos, chilled a bit with Tyler,

00:00:52.840 --> 00:00:55.960
"I got a big question for you." "Wha-?" "Explain the cloud."

00:00:55.960 --> 00:00:59.640
Then went to the They Might Be Giants concert, where I ran into Steve Zaragoza from SourceFed,

00:00:59.640 --> 00:01:04.220
had breakfast with friends, then spent a full day at a collab camp, which is a totally new idea to me

00:01:04.220 --> 00:01:08.000
but where I met a ton of YouTubers, and then had dinner with Jake and Michael of Vsauce,

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:11.360
spent a full day at BuzzFeed, where I made a bunch of stuff and talked to a bunch of cool people

00:01:11.380 --> 00:01:15.260
but only filmed this one clip, shot a thing Google's working on, had lunch with Mayim Bialik,

00:01:15.260 --> 00:01:18.100
then went to 3 Black Dot to talk shop and play with the HTC Vive,

00:01:18.100 --> 00:01:22.480
then had dinner wth MatPat of The Game Theorists, went shopping with HartBeat and Foxy at the Grove,

00:01:22.480 --> 00:01:25.880
had a quick chat with Markiplier, followed by dinner with Hannah Hart, her sister Maggie, and Mitchell Davis

00:01:25.900 --> 00:01:31.100
and I still have so much more to do: shooting YouTubers Reacts, recording with the Gilmore Guys and Travis McElroy,

00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:35.400
more fun, more friends. John, I am a fan.

00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:41.760
I'm a careful fan, but once I am a fan, I am an unabashed fan. There's an element in my appreciation

00:01:41.760 --> 00:01:47.280
of other people's work that's more of like, I want to be like them, I want to make things as good as what they make.

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:53.920
And I think that's where some of my ambition comes from, but I also just simply enjoy liking them

00:01:53.920 --> 00:02:00.680
and the things they make. I like liking that stuff. Sometimes 'I like you' gets caught up with

00:02:00.680 --> 00:02:06.580
'I want to be like you', but those things are not the same thing, and realizing that has been a really big deal for me.

00:02:06.580 --> 00:02:12.820
I really enjoyed this trip, but I do not want to live in LA because I do not want this fortnight to be normal.

00:02:12.820 --> 00:02:19.660
I need to be a step away. Being an observational fan is, in a lot of ways, better than being inside.

00:02:19.660 --> 00:02:24.920
I never wanna love the 'fan' bit, otherwise these last weeks would not have been as invigorating

00:02:24.920 --> 00:02:31.200
or inspiring as they have. I am a fan of the things these people create, I am a fan of the fact that the internet

00:02:31.260 --> 00:02:38.260
has allowed them to do it. I'm just so pleased, and feel so lucky. I get to be friends with the people I'm fans of.

00:02:38.260 --> 00:02:43.800
And in one case, I get to be brothers with them, too. Which maybe makes me the luckiest fan ever.

00:02:43.800 --> 00:02:45.720
John, I'll see you on Tuesday.

